{
  "name": "Manifest Mind",
  "type": "feat",
  "_id": "D9NBAXxFBdPamwEt",
  "img": "icons/magic/perception/eye-ringed-glow-angry-large-teal.webp",
  "folder": "ghLCKXUvXMt4WBiM",
  "sort": 300000,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You can conjure the mind of your Awakened Spellbook. As a Bonus Action while the book is on your person, you can make the mind manifest as a Tiny spectral object hovering in an unoccupied space of your choice within 60 feet of you. It is intangible, doesn't occupy its space, sheds Dim Light in a 10-foot radius, and looks like a ghostly tome, a cascade of text, or a scholar from the past (your choice). While manifested, it can hear and see, has Darkvision with a range of 60 feet, and can telepathically share what it sees and hears with you (no action required).</p><p>Whenever you cast a Wizard spell on your turn, you can cast it as if you were in the spectral mind's space, using its senses. You can do so a number of times per day equal to your Proficiency Bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest. As a Bonus Action, you can make the mind hover up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you or it can see; it can pass through creatures but not objects.</p><p>The mind stops manifesting if it is ever more than 300 feet from you, if someone casts Dispel Magic on it, if the Awakened Spellbook is destroyed, if you die, or if you dismiss it as a Bonus Action. Once you conjure it, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest, unless you expend a spell slot of any level to conjure it again.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
